WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.932
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.232 --> 00:00:08.630
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:13.986
Unit thirteen: Conclusions. Today you will finish an essay with a strong conclusion.

4
00:00:14.286 --> 00:00:16.880
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:17.833 --> 00:00:20.857
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:21.717 --> 00:00:22.671
Conclusion.

7
00:00:23.683 --> 00:00:26.240
Conclusion means the final part of an essay.

8
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:28.606
Write a strong conclusion.

9
00:00:29.217 --> 00:00:31.579
Your turn. Say: Conclusion.

10
00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:35.620
Conclusion.

11
00:00:36.383 --> 00:00:37.640
Summarise.

12
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:41.485
Summarise means to repeat main points briefly.

13
00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:43.711
Summarise your argument.

14
00:00:44.317 --> 00:00:47.108
Your turn. Say: Summarise.

15
00:00:49.967 --> 00:00:51.165
Summarise.

16
00:00:51.917 --> 00:00:52.778
Restate.

17
00:00:53.783 --> 00:00:56.433
Restate means to say again in different words.

18
00:00:57.017 --> 00:00:58.505
Restate your thesis.

19
00:00:59.117 --> 00:01:01.479
Your turn. Say: Restate.

20
00:01:04.333 --> 00:01:05.207
Restate.

21
00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.230
In conclusion.

22
00:01:08.217 --> 00:01:11.029
In conclusion means a phrase that signals the end.

23
00:01:11.617 --> 00:01:14.034
In conclusion, trees help cities.

24
00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:17.209
Your turn. Say: In conclusion.

25
00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:21.010
In conclusion.

26
00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.076
Recommendation.

27
00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:26.930
Recommendation means advice about what to do.

28
00:01:27.517 --> 00:01:29.156
End with a recommendation.

29
00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.414
Your turn. Say: Recommendation.

30
00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:36.616
Recommendation.

31
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:38.351
Overall.

32
00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:41.744
Overall means considering everything.

33
00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:44.222
Overall, the plan is good.

34
00:01:44.817 --> 00:01:47.376
Your turn. Say: Overall.

35
00:01:50.233 --> 00:01:51.223
Overall.

36
00:01:51.983 --> 00:01:53.089
Final thought.

37
00:01:54.083 --> 00:01:56.594
Final thought means a last idea for the reader.

38
00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.579
Give a final thought.

39
00:01:59.183 --> 00:02:01.940
Your turn. Say: Final thought.

40
00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:05.952
Final thought.

41
00:02:06.717 --> 00:02:07.799
Introduce.

42
00:02:08.783 --> 00:02:11.027
Introduce means to bring in something new.

43
00:02:11.617 --> 00:02:13.628
Do not introduce new ideas.

44
00:02:14.217 --> 00:02:16.997
Your turn. Say: Introduce.

45
00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:20.939
Introduce.

46
00:02:21.733 --> 00:02:25.465
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.317 --> 00:02:28.606
Visal, what should a conclusion do?

48
00:02:29.717 --> 00:02:37.080
It should restate your thesis in different words, summarise your main points and leave the reader with a final thought.

49
00:02:38.183 --> 00:02:39.614
Can I add a new idea?

50
00:02:40.717 --> 00:02:46.576
No. Never introduce new ideas in the conclusion. It confuses the reader.

51
00:02:47.683 --> 00:02:49.126
Which phrases help?

52
00:02:50.217 --> 00:02:58.929
Use in conclusion, overall or to sum up. Then give a recommendation, for example, cities should act now.

53
00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:01.509
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:05.151
Grammar focus: Conclusion phrases.

55
00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:06.637
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:12.182
In conclusion, trees make cities healthier, so every city should plant more.

57
00:03:13.083 --> 00:03:17.300
Overall, reading builds skills, so students should read daily.

58
00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:24.448
Restate the thesis in new words, summarise the main points and end with a final thought. Do not add new ideas.

59
00:03:25.183 --> 00:03:28.544
Be careful! Don't say: In conclusion, also, new idea.

60
00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:33.115
Say: In conclusion, trees help cities.

61
00:03:33.415 --> 00:03:35.136
Do not add new ideas.

62
00:03:35.933 --> 00:03:38.597
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:40.529
Ending the Essay.

64
00:03:40.829 --> 00:03:42.701
Bopha reaches the end of her essay.

65
00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.756
She writes In conclusion and restates her thesis.

66
00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:50.161
She summarises her two main points.

67
00:03:51.167 --> 00:03:54.060
She ends with a recommendation to the city council.

68
00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:56.811
She adds no new ideas.

69
00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:02.204
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:05.050
The conclusion is the blank part.

71
00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:08.434
A, middle. B, last. C, first.

72
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.953
The answer is B: last.

73
00:04:15.117 --> 00:04:17.557
Restate means say again in blank words.

74
00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:21.267
A, same. B, no. C, different.

75
00:04:24.833 --> 00:04:26.589
The answer is C: different.

76
00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:30.527
Summarise means to repeat main points blank.

77
00:04:30.827 --> 00:04:34.191
A, briefly. B, slowly. C, loudly.

78
00:04:37.733 --> 00:04:39.652
The answer is A: briefly.

79
00:04:40.817 --> 00:04:42.630
Never add a blank idea.

80
00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:46.282
A, short. B, new. C, good.

81
00:04:49.833 --> 00:04:51.427
The answer is B: new.

82
00:04:52.583 --> 00:04:54.223
Bopha ends with a blank.

83
00:04:54.523 --> 00:04:58.525
A, joke. B, recipe. C, recommendation.

84
00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:04.670
The answer is C: recommendation.

85
00:05:05.867 --> 00:05:09.007
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:11.675
How do you write a conclusion?

87
00:05:20.483 --> 00:05:21.960
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:34.354
I start with in conclusion and restate my thesis in different words. I summarise the main points and finish with a recommendation or a final thought. I never add new ideas.

89
00:05:34.654 --> 00:05:36.445
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:41.790
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and conclusion phrases.

91
00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:47.227
Today's value is mastery. Practise with patience until your skill becomes excellence.

92
00:05:47.527 --> 00:05:50.098
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:50.398 --> 00:05:52.923
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

